{"name":"Ordain","hex":"#998188","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ordain","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prearrange unalterably.","To decree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ordain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ordination","blocks":[{"text":"Ordination is the process by which individuals are consecrated, that is, set apart and elevated from the laity class to the clergy, who are thus then authorized to perform various religious rites and ceremonies. The process and ceremonies of ordination may vary by religion and denomination. One who is in preparation for, or who is undergoing, the process of ordination is sometimes called an ordinand. The liturgy used at an ordination is commonly found in a book known as an Ordinal which provides the ordo for celebrations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Ordination_of_a_deacon_1520.jpg/330px-Ordination_of_a_deacon_1520.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ordination","wikidata":"Q7519600"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Priestly_ordination.jpg/250px-Priestly_ordination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/30/Priestly_ordination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Priestly_ordination.jpg/250px-Priestly_ordination.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ordination of a Catholic priest in the extraordinary form of the Roman Rite, 2007","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APriestly_ordination.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg/500px-Pr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg/1280px-Pr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg/500px-Pr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The ordination of Lutheran priests and deacons in Stockholm Cathedral","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APr%C3%A4stvigning_Storkyrkan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Cheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg/500px-Cheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Cheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg/1280px-Cheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Cheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg/500px-Cheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ordination of an Orthodox. The deacon being ordained is kneeling with the bishop's omophorion over his head as the bishop blesses him immediately before the Cheirotonia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACheirotonia_Presbyter_3.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Kheirotonia.jpg/500px-Kheirotonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Kheirotonia.jpg/1280px-Kheirotonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Kheirotonia.jpg/500px-Kheirotonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eastern Orth